<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mutsu Munemitsu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1897</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mutsu Munemitsu was a Japanese statesman from the Kii domain who served as foreign minister from 1892 to 1896. He negotiated the Anglo-Japanese Treaty of Commerce and Navigation of 1894, which ended British extraterritoriality in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi">Itō Hirobumi</a> concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shimonoseki">Treaty of Shimonoseki</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a>. His memoir Kenkenroku recounts the diplomacy of that war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mutsu-munemitsu.jpg" alt="Mutsu Munemitsu" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutsu_Munemitsu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
